  "notes": "Recorded GAAP-style like FY2023/FY2024 (governmental funds modified cash, fund-balance roll-forward; business-type accrual). Governmental lines from Total Governmental Funds (p5): 527,367 + 619,633 - 612,756 + Transfer from CRA 35,542 = 569,786; the Total column prints fund transfers in(out) as '-'. Beginning cash not printed (null). ending_cash = cash 513,931 + county treasurer cash 11,907 (p4, as FY2023); certificate of deposit 43,948 in ending_investments. Business-type from the proprietary statement Total column (p7): 625,801 + 1,354,809 - 1,125,379 + transfers net 0 = 855,231; expenses 1,125,379 = Statement of Activities total business-type (p2). Proprietary cash flows Total column pp8-9. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), Governmental / Business-type columns (component unit excluded). Detail: General Fund revenue and department totals from the GF budgetary comparison schedule (p10); the GF departments combining schedule (p14) gives object lines for General, Police, Pool and Park; its continuation page (Fire, Ambulance, Library, Community Center columns and totals, report p53) is not in the trimmed PDF, so those four departments are recorded as not-itemized totals from p10 (no double counting; GF expenditure items tie to 331,115). Street, Sales Tax budget schedules (pp11-12) and nonmajor combining (CDBG, Keno; p13) recorded per fund. No business-type schedules (no business-type detail, as FY2023/FY2024). Read pages 1-14 of 14"
